Ok, I don't know if this the proper list to ask this, but...

I'm fairly new to Debian, and I have sarge running in a couple of alpha 
machines.

Today we had a power failure, followed by some network problems (the 
switch to which our DHCP server is connected, went into a coma...), but 
when things were put back to normal, our alpha machines (the only ones 
running Debian) had to have their network interfaces restarted manually 
in order to get an IP address.

Is this normal, shouldn't dhclient on Debian go into the background and 
configure the interfaces as soon as a DHCP server gets available, like 
other distros (SuSE, for instance) do?

If this is normal behaviour, is there some way to change it (I'm not 
asking about going around changing scripts)?

Carlos Rodrigues



